import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout path="/about/" title="About Number Spinner — How Our Random Tools Work" description="How Number Spinner uses browser Web Crypto, unbiased integer sampling, optional weights and no-repeat draws; learn the limits and inspect source code.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our methods and limits</span>
    <h1>How Number Spinner works</h1>
    <p>Free, browser-based random selection tools for names, numbers, classroom activities and everyday choices. Here is what they do—and what they do not claim to do.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article geo-methodology">
    <h2 id="how-results-are-generated">How results are generated</h2>
    <p>Number Spinner's core random selection runs in your browser. It obtains random bytes through the browser's <code>crypto.getRandomValues()</code> API and uses rejection sampling when mapping random integers into the number of eligible choices. Rejection sampling avoids the small distribution bias that can arise from a simple modulo operation.</p>
    <p>The number is chosen by the random-selection code, not by the visible animation. The animated wheel is a way to reveal the result. When a range contains many numbers, the graphic uses a simplified set of colored slices; the full eligible number pool remains available to the picker.</p>
    <h3>Equal chances versus weighted choices</h3>
    <p>For a fresh independent draw from 1 through 100 with no exclusions and a step of 1, each number has a probability of 1/100 (1%). The same principle applies to other inclusive number ranges. With a range of 1–20 but three numbers excluded, each of the remaining 17 numbers has a 1/17 chance on a new independent draw.</p>
    <p>For custom names or choices, each entry starts at weight 1. Writing <code>Pizza | 3</code> gives that entry three times the selection weight of an entry at weight 1; this is not a guarantee of any outcome. Repeating the same name on separate lines creates separate entries.</p>
    <h3>Drawing without replacement</h3>
    <p>When Remove winners is on, an already selected entry is not selected again in that round. You can also generate a batch of 1–100 results. If you need unique values, enable Remove winners before drawing the batch; if repeats are allowed, each draw may select the same value again. Reset starts a new round.</p>

    <h2>What is available, and what are the limits?</h2>
    <dl class="geo-method-list">
      <div><dt>Number range</dt><dd>Whole-number ranges with a positive step and up to 10,000 eligible values before exclusions.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Batch selection</dt><dd>Up to 100 picks per draw; uniqueness depends on the Remove winners setting and available choices.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Privacy</dt><dd>Choice processing happens locally in the browser. Optional saved configurations use localStorage; sharing a setup places its content into the link fragment, visible to anyone you share it with.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Reliability</dt><dd>Results depend on a functioning browser Web Crypto implementation. This website is not an independently audited or certified lottery, cryptographic key generator, or regulated prize-drawing service.</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <h2 id="sources-and-corrections">Inspectable implementation and corrections</h2>
    <p>These descriptions are based on the site's publicly readable implementation, rather than claimed customer counts or unverifiable randomness certifications. Inspect the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Random-Wheel/blob/main/src/lib/random.ts">random number and weighting algorithms</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Random-Wheel/blob/main/src/scripts/wheel.ts">wheel interaction and result logic</a>. The browser API itself is described by <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Crypto/getRandomValues">MDN's Crypto.getRandomValues reference</a>.</p>
    <p>For a reproducible bug or factual correction, open a report in the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Random-Wheel/issues">public issue tracker</a> or see <a href="/contact/">contact options</a>. Do not put private names, student records, or sensitive information into public reports.</p>
    <p>These technical details describe the current general-purpose tool; source availability does not imply any independent security audit. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for hosting, link sharing and local storage information.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
